# Assignment 7 follows A6's upload rule (user, 2026-11-07): the full game lives
# here on disk so it runs, but git tracks only what the assignment asks for.
# Everything is ignored by default. The game files a reviewer needs to open and
# run the project (scripts/a7_tracked_files.py: the export whitelist, its
# .import/.uid sidecars, tests/ and scripts/) are added explicitly with
# `git add -f`; A7's own new paths are listed back in below.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/*.md
!/scripts/
!/effects/
!/animations/
!/tools/
!/previews/
!/captures/
!/prompts/
!/sessions/
!/evidence/
!/youtube/
# Game files A7 reads or changes (their starting version is committed first)
!/project.godot
!/shaders/
/shaders/*
!/shaders/particles_generated.gdshader*
!/tests/
!/tests/**
/tests/**/*.log
# Cited logs only
!/logs/
/logs/*
!/logs/baseline-*/
/logs/baseline-*/*
!/logs/baseline-*/summary.txt
!/logs/a7_*.log
!/logs/test_a7_*.log
!/logs/test_npc_idle*.log
!/logs/test_wave_*.log
!/logs/a7_mutations/
/logs/a7_mutations/*.import.log
# Film media never goes to GitHub
*.mp4
*.mp3
*.wav
*.mov
.godot/

# Full agent transcripts are over ~1 MB: kept locally, excerpts are committed
/sessions/session-?.jsonl
